`Upload.create` always marks `is_used`, sets a default `multiple`, normalizes `class_name`, filters `supported_props`, ensures an `id`, synthesizes `on_drop` when absent, memoizes the event trigger, camel-cases `upload_props`, builds `useDropzone` hook data, creates the input, creates the box/zone, attaches root props, and returns `super().create(zone)`. Across the 10 tests, only the `if upload_props.get("on_drop") is None` branch is exercised; the `else` block for user-supplied `on_drop` is never taken. The tests also cover both outcomes of `if isinstance(given_class_name, str)` indirectly only as false (list or missing), so that inner body is not covered, while the rest of the method body is reached in every case, including variants with extra non-upload props and children.

